      "Language": "ger",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Left ventricular non-compaction is an unclassified cardiomyopathy characterized by an excessively prominent trabecular meshwork due to an arrest in myocardial morphogenesis. We report on a 51-year-old female patient with abnormal myocardial trabeculations associated with a congenital mitral valve stenosis post commissurotomy at the age of 14. In the present case report, clinical manifestation of the disorder included impaired left ventricular systolic function and atrial fibrillation. Noncompaction was diagnosed by echocardiography and levocardiography. In addition, a review of the literature on this rare disorder is presented."},
